  "proof_notes": {
    "partition_bound_lemma": "For every part m>=2, (m+1) <= 3*2^(m-2). Singleton parts contribute factor 2. For k>=1 nontrivial parts, multiplying gives Q <= 3^k*2^(n-2k) <= 3*2^(n-2) because (3/4)^(k-1)<=1.",
    "strict_compression_lemma": "3*2^(n-2) = (3/4)*2^n < 2^n.",
    "group_lemma": "Transpositions associated with edges of any connected graph generate the full symmetric group on its vertices; the frozen connected_cells graph is connected by construction on each cell.",
    "orbit_lemma": "The full symmetric group on a Boolean cell acts transitively on assignments of equal Hamming weight, so one representative for each count 0..|C| is complete.",
    "control_flow_lemma": "With a nontrivial cell, Q<=L^2, and Q<2^n, all three pre-admission OPEN branches are excluded; finite quotient enumeration returns SAT at the first satisfying representative or UNSAT after exactly Q representatives."
  },
